# ==== T-FMT-C · a RUN of blanks between nested `meta if` items collapses to one
#
# The run-collapse half of the nested-item blank rule, and the one cell of that
# axis that cannot be a fixpoint fixture — its whole point is that the input and
# the output differ. Compared against the `.expected` companion.
#
# Preserving author blanks must not mean preserving however many the author
# left: the rule at every level is "a blank iff one was written, runs collapse
# to one", which is what `format_module` and `format_block_stmts` already do.
# Three blank lines between two nested definitions come back as one.
#
# The sibling cells — blank preserved per branch, and no blank staying absent —
# are in `meta_if_nested_item_blanks.gg`.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11): the blanks were not collapsed to one, they
#   were deleted outright, so this file came back with the two definitions
#   welded together.

meta if platform() == "macos":
    int alpha():
        return 1

    int beta():
        return 2
else:
    int alpha():
        return 3

    int beta():
        return 4

void main():
    print(alpha())
    print(beta())
